mastery.solution_text:
Translate $y = \sqrt{x}$ left $9$ units and down $3$ units.
Endpoint: $(-9, -3)$.
The points $(0,0), (1,1), (4,2), (9,3)$ become $(-9,-3), (-8,-2), (-5,-1), (0,0)$.
At $x = 0$, $y = \sqrt{9} - 3 = 0$.
At $y = 0$, $\sqrt{x + 9} = 3 \implies x + 9 = 9 \implies x = 0$.
Both intercepts are $(0,0)$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.45]
\draw[->] (-10,0) -- (3,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-4) -- (0,2) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[thick,-{Stealth}] plot[domain=0:3.4,samples=101,smooth,variable=\t] ({-9+\t*\t},{-3+\t});
\fill (-9,-3) circle (3pt) node[below right] {$(-9,-3)$};
\fill (-8,-2) circle (2pt);
\fill (-5,-1) circle (2pt);
\fill (0,0) circle (2pt) node[above left] {$(0,0)$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

